<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδεκ-τέον</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδέχομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must
				receive from others,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ εἰσφερόμενα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					7.36
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one must accept, allow, admit,</i> c. acc. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					668a
				</span></i>
			: c. gen. et part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὸς λέγοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					160c
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				379c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ἄλλως ἀ. λεγομένης τέχνης;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					272b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span> Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				329.16
			</span></i>, Zos.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.229B.
			</span></i></div>
